<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 261)</h2>
<p><b>Share to Web is here.</b> Send a review to anyone with a browser — Windows, locked-down laptops, no install.</p>
<ul>
<li><b>File → Share to Web…</b> while hosting a shared review: the current clip becomes an encrypted review proxy and you get a link. The person who opens it can play, frame-step, <b>comment and draw</b> — everything comes back into your session live, attributed, exactly like a native guest. If they open it after the meeting instead, their notes wait for you.</li>
<li>They follow your playhead during a live session, can unlatch to look around, and relatch with one click. Concurrent markup merges — nobody's marks are lost.</li>
<li><b>Sensitive share?</b> Toggle "require a passphrase" and read the four generated words on the call — the link alone is useless. An optional setting lets their browser keep an encrypted copy so they can revisit the review after it ends; <b>End Review</b> wipes the cloud either way.</li>
<li>Everything is end-to-end encrypted — the relay and storage only ever see ciphertext. Mac users who open a web link are pointed to the full app instead.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
